{
  "id": "fluid_flow___equivalent_diameter",
  "title": "Fluid Flow - Equivalent Diameter",
  "description": "Calculate the equivalent diameter of rectangular, oval, and oblong ducts or pipes. The equivalent diameter is the diameter of a circular duct that produces the same pressure loss as an equivalent rectangular duct for equal flow.",
  "type": "datatable",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Rectangular Duct Equivalent Diameter Calculator\n\n**Formula (Huebscher):**\n\n_de = 1.30 (a × b)^0.625 / (a + b)^0.25_\n\nWhere:\n- **de** = equivalent diameter (mm or inches)\n- **a** = length of major or minor side (mm or inches)\n- **b** = length of minor or major side (mm or inches)\n\nA round shape results in lower pressure drops and less fan horsepower."
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "side_a",
          "label": "Duct Side a",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 300,
          "unit": "mm"
        },
        {
          "id": "side_b",
          "label": "Duct Side b",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 500,
          "unit": "mm"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "equiv_diameter",
          "label": "Equivalent Diameter",
          "formula": "1.30 * Math.pow(inputs.side_a * inputs.side_b, 0.625) / Math.pow(inputs.side_a + inputs.side_b, 0.25)",
          "unit": "mm",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
