    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Oval Duct (Ellipse) Equivalent Diameter\n\n**Formula (Heyt & Diaz):**\n\n_de = 1.55 × A^0.625 / P^0.25_\n\nWhere:\n- **A** = cross-sectional area (m² or in²)\n- **P** = perimeter (m or inches)\n- **A = π × a × b / 4**\n- **P ≈ 2π × √((a/2)² + (b/2)²) / 2**\n\nWhere a = major dimension, b = minor dimension"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Oblong Duct Equivalent Diameter\n\n**Formula:**\n\n_de = 1.55 × (π × b² / 4 + a × b - b²)^0.625 / (π × b + 2 × a - 2 × b)^0.25_\n\nWhere a and b are the dimensions of the oblong duct."
    }
